{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110441","id":2821213295,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6oKExv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110441","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110441.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110441.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110441","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110441/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110441/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110441/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/3564170918c03a618a55fa7b3e0f58b0817259e6","number":110441,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Implement LibGodot, a currently-minimal API to embed Godot as a library.","user":{"login":"zorbathut","id":160754,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MDc1NA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/160754?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut","html_url":"https://github.com/zorbathut","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zorbathut/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# What is it?\r\n\r\nLibGodot allows you to embed Godot into a program as a library and control Godot directly, instead of expecting Godot to be the coordinator and overseer.\r\n\r\n# Why?\r\n\r\nHere's a not-comprehensive list of reasons you might want to do this.\r\n\r\n* Run Godot Engine from a host application that, for whatever reason, can't be made a client of Godot.\r\n* Write scripts for automation of development tasks.\r\n* Embed Godot into another application while displaying Godot Windows as part of the host application's UI.\r\n\r\nAs an example, the author has been using an earlier version of this for native C# tests. The C# test APIs can't run the Godot binary directly, they *must* be run within a native .NET environment, but by running Godot as a library within that .NET environment, C# testing is made far easier.\r\n\r\nOther people have integrated Godot into Blender and Unreal Engine for their own reasons.\r\n\r\n# Features\r\n\r\nThis is a minimum-viable-product of the basic concepts of LibGodot. It includes:\r\n\r\n* Shared library support\r\n* Windows and Linux support\r\n* One-time startup and shutdown functionality\r\n* Direct control over the update loop\r\n* Headless and Godot-window support\r\n\r\nIt does not yet include:\r\n\r\n* Static library support\r\n* Mac, smartphone, or other platform support\r\n* Repeated clean startups and shutdowns\r\n* Starting from C#\r\n* Embedding the viewport in a custom window\r\n* Github Actions compilation tests\r\n\r\nI plan to include several of these as followup PRs in the near future, but this is complicated enough as-is; in addition, getting the foundation in place allows others to contribute features, especially for things I can't do on my own like Mac support.\r\n\r\n# How do I try it?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/zorbathut/libgodot_example\r\n\r\nThis contains a miniscule Godot project; one scene with a Label, and a C++ program that starts Godot as a shared library. The C++ framework finds and modifies the label at runtime for ten seconds, then shuts down on its own. Porting the C++ program to other languages should be reasonably easy (as long as they support GDExtension.)\r\n\r\n# Details . . .\r\n\r\n. . . are long and complicated. I can talk at great length about some of the decisions I made here and why I diverged from kisg's original patch. I could probably write an entire small novel that nobody would read. Ask questions!\r\n\r\nI will note that the name \"libgodot\" isn't great because some people are already using this for GDExtension APIs. I don't have a better name though. Happy to change it.\r\n\r\n# Credits\r\n\r\nThis has been built on the work of multiple people, including:\r\n\r\n@Faolan-Rad - https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72883\r\n@kisg - https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90510\r\n@fire - considerable support on Discord\r\n\r\nThere's probably people I'm missing, because this has been bouncing around for two years now. Let me know if someone should be added (or wants to be removed).\r\n\r\nThis supercedes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/72883 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/90510, and closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/6267.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":580537003,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODA1MzcwMDM=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gdextension","name":"topic:gdextension","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-09-12T04:36:47Z","updated_at